{"approved":false,"back_sample":null,"beam_size":2,"checks":{"no_residual_markers":false,"nonempty":true,"not_truncated":true,"protected_values":false,"translated":true},"context":"effective-interest-rate-calculator UI copy.howAnswer","detected_language":"nl","format":"usefulverse-background-draft-v1","key":"effective-interest-rate-calculator.copy.howAnswer","keys":["effective-interest-rate-calculator.copy.howAnswer"],"locale":"nl","model":"google/madlad400-3b-mt","raw_translation":"Voor periodieke samenstelling is JKP = (ZXQPH0000QXZ + JKP ÷ m)^m − ZXQPH0001QXZ, waarbij m het aantal samenstellingsperioden per jaar is. Om JKP terug te zetten naar nominaal JKP, gebruikt u JKP = m × ((ZXQPH0002QXZ + JKP)^(ZXQPH0003QXZ/m) − ZXQPH0004QXZ). Voor continue samenstelling wordt JKP = e^JKP − ZXQPH0005QXZ gebruikt.","record_id":"f650fa2328d51984a4f22eba69c2273c7d09582845f16f44522abc3d5e976d0e","revision":"fa184c675da0b5c9e1c8694fccd4e12e2d422094","run_id":"40565692987","seconds":2.741708455749972,"source":"For periodic compounding, APY = (1 + APR ÷ m)^m − 1, where m is the number of compounding periods per year. To convert APY back to nominal APR, use APR = m × ((1 + APY)^(1/m) − 1). Continuous compounding uses APY = e^APR − 1. Enter rates as percentages; for example, 12 means 12%.","source_commit":"e8a7cb94dc75d40f2c0e14bb27c0a1819e230012","source_hash":"fe78b074adbd1d99e0a797d7cf4aab3016d94b38ff9812d5eef74ae6613339fa","status":"needs-review","translation":"Voor periodieke samenstelling is JKP = (ZXQPH0000QXZ + JKP ÷ m)^m − ZXQPH0001QXZ, waarbij m het aantal samenstellingsperioden per jaar is. Om JKP terug te zetten naar nominaal JKP, gebruikt u JKP = m × ((ZXQPH0002QXZ + JKP)^(ZXQPH0003QXZ/m) − ZXQPH0004QXZ). Voor continue samenstelling wordt JKP = e^JKP − ZXQPH0005QXZ gebruikt.","truncated":false,"warnings":[]}
